    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 141938\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n1238 PM PDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Breezy south-southwesterly wind gusts will continue through the\n  week with dry conditions and near-normal temperatures.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Persistent troughing across the Western US will keep\nthe region in a generally dry and breezy pattern through much of\nthe upcoming week. In the near term, a trough will eject into the\nNorthern Plains today before additional troughing drops south\nalong the Pacific Northwest Coast by midweek. This will keep the\nMojave Desert and southern Great Basin region in a southwesterly\nflow aloft, favoring breezy conditions in the afternoons and any\nlingering monsoonal moisture focused more across central and\neastern Arizona. A few isolated thunderstorms may develop across\neastern Mohave County through midweek, but coverage is expected \nto be quite limited. \n\nOtherwise, thanks to the pattern at hand, temperatures will remain\nnear seasonal normals through the period. The flow pattern will\ntrend more zonal by the weekend allowing for the gusty winds to\nease while temperatures remain near normal. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Gusty\nsouth-southwesterly winds will pick up t his morning, with gusts to \n20-25KT expected through sunset this evening. Thereafter, sustained \nspeeds will remain around 10KT through Tuesday morning before gusty \nwinds return in the late morning and afternoon. VFR conditions \nprevail, with temperatures briefly reaching a high of 100 degrees \naround 23Z-00Z.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Winds across much of the \nregion will become elevated and gusty out of the south-southwest by \nmid- to late morning, with gusts to 20-25KT common through this \nevening before gradually diminishing. Exceptions include the western \nMojave Desert/KDAG, where west-northwesterly winds are not expected \nto shift to the southwest until early evening, with gusts continuing \nthrough much of the night, as well as the northern Owens \nValley/KBIH, where winds generally follow typical daily patterns \nwith speeds around 10KT or less. VFR conditions will prevail, with \nisolated thunderstorms expected over portions of northwestern \nArizona this afternoon that are unlikely to cause any impacts at \narea terminals.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION/AVIATION...Outler\n\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
